<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>International news from the Americas - France 24</title><description>FRANCE 24’s coverage of the political, social and economic issues in the United States, Canada, Mexico, Argentina, Brazil and across the Americas.</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/</link><lastBuildDate>Tue, 15 Sep 2026 08:04:10 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>Spotlight</category><title>Corruption ‘endemic’ in Trump administration: 'Checks and balances only in effect at lower courts'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260915-corruption-endemic-in-trump-administration-checks-and-balances-only-in-effect-at-lower-courts</link><description>
François Picard is pleased to welcome Andrew Weissmann, Author, Professor at NYU School of Law, and former General Counsel of the FBI. He argues that as political deception and deliberate falsehoods become normalized, and politically useful, it erodes any trust we have in our government and our institutions. Drawing on his book, "Liar’s Kingdom", Weissmann questions why political leaders are above the law in the United States, while ordinary citizens risk serious legal consequences for making intentionally false statements.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/134880ea-b0b3-11f1-871a-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260914-180947-182810-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/134880ea-b0b3-11f1-871a-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260914-180947-182810-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">74a4dd9e-b0da-11f1-9bd1-b95f3054049f</guid><pubDate>Tue, 15 Sep 2026 07:52:51 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>François PICARD</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Iran war exposes US munitions shortfall, industrial bottlenecks, Pentagon report says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260915-iran-war-exposes-us-munitions-shortfall-industrial-bottlenecks-pentagon-report-says</link><description>
The US military faces shortages of key munitions due to the Iran war and industrial "bottlenecks" to rebuild stockpiles, a Pentagon watchdog warned in a report published on Monday, contradicting US President Donald Trump's assurances that ammunition supplies are "virtually unlimited".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/76716e8e-b0c7-11f1-9d6d-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C8744CR.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/76716e8e-b0c7-11f1-9d6d-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C8744CR.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">26def974-b0ca-11f1-8bd4-757e8e613dcc</guid><pubDate>Tue, 15 Sep 2026 06:07:23 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/76716e8e-b0c7-11f1-9d6d-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C8744CR.jpg">© US Navy via AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Venezuela to join G20 energy talks in Texas at US invitation</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260915-venezuela-to-join-g20-energy-meetings-in-texas-at-us-invitation</link><description>
A Venezuelan delegation will join G20 energy talks in Houston this week as soaring oil prices and disruption from the Middle East war put global energy supplies under pressure. The meeting comes as the Trump administration deepens energy ties with Caracas and seeks to boost Venezuelan oil output.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/47d96d1c-b098-11f1-9021-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/ea7607de8aa30c2ff2134ead7b6e53246246fe8f.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/47d96d1c-b098-11f1-9021-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/ea7607de8aa30c2ff2134ead7b6e53246246fe8f.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6a5aff92-b0af-11f1-8158-3570f775cb63</guid><pubDate>Tue, 15 Sep 2026 02:44:46 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/47d96d1c-b098-11f1-9021-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/ea7607de8aa30c2ff2134ead7b6e53246246fe8f.jpg">© Ronaldo Schemidt, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>US Supreme Court rejects Trump bid to restrict mail ballots as voting begins</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260915-us-supreme-court-rejects-trump-bid-to-restrict-mail-ballots-as-voting-begins</link><description>
The US Supreme Court on Monday rejected President Donald Trump’s bid to impose new restrictions on mail ballots ahead of November’s midterm elections. The ruling leaves states free to continue using existing voting procedures, after election officials warned the last-minute changes could disrupt ballot distribution.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/def44e4c-b09d-11f1-be01-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/bb30b5bf37e781f443665b25112221e81b7c2d36.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/def44e4c-b09d-11f1-be01-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/bb30b5bf37e781f443665b25112221e81b7c2d36.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f7fd1a90-b0a2-11f1-b996-bf02f22ad66f</guid><pubDate>Tue, 15 Sep 2026 01:51:51 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/def44e4c-b09d-11f1-be01-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/bb30b5bf37e781f443665b25112221e81b7c2d36.jpg">© Saul Loeb, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Rapper Macklemore dropped from Ed Sheeran's US tour after pro-Palestinian remarks</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260914-macklemore-dropped-from-ed-sheeran-us-tour-after-pro-palestinian-remarks</link><description>
American rapper Macklemore announced Monday that he was dropped from British singer Ed Sheeran’s US stadium tour after saying "Free Palestine" during a September 4 concert in New Jersey. The Grammy winner’s removal follows pressure from venue owners, including New England Patriots owner Robert Kraft, over his criticism of Israel’s actions in Gaza.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6d38d806-b078-11f1-b9cc-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/1729ad2e072996a142da7b053ef29307fba83d5a.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6d38d806-b078-11f1-b9cc-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/1729ad2e072996a142da7b053ef29307fba83d5a.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">83b4b46c-b08a-11f1-b5e0-b3452f437d0f</guid><pubDate>Mon, 14 Sep 2026 22:20:37 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6d38d806-b078-11f1-b9cc-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/1729ad2e072996a142da7b053ef29307fba83d5a.jpg">© Arnaud Finistre, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>US Space Force confirms weapons deployed in space for first time</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260914-us-space-force-confirms-weapons-deployed-in-space-for-first-time</link><description>
The US Space Force on Monday confirmed for the first time that Washington has weapons deployed in orbit, as the United States, China and Russia expand their military capabilities in space. The disclosure highlights a growing focus on controlling the space domain and protecting satellites vital to military communications, surveillance and navigation.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/54b1beee-a432-11f1-8b6d-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-29T195602Z-94810877-RC2I8NAYVGKF-RTRMADP-3-SPACE-NASA-TELESCOPE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/54b1beee-a432-11f1-8b6d-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-29T195602Z-94810877-RC2I8NAYVGKF-RTRMADP-3-SPACE-NASA-TELESCOPE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">22322948-b087-11f1-ad6a-db263a3e2d74</guid><pubDate>Mon, 14 Sep 2026 21:56:25 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/54b1beee-a432-11f1-8b6d-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-29T195602Z-94810877-RC2I8NAYVGKF-RTRMADP-3-SPACE-NASA-TELESCOPE.jpg">© Joe Skipper, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Trump criticises 'negative forces' seeking to slow AI development</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260914-trump-criticises-negative-forces-seeking-to-slow-ai-development</link><description>
US President Donald Trump on Sunday slammed critics of artificial intelligence (AI) who warned firms to slow down development, branding them "negative" forces. The comments came soon after OpenAI CEO Sam Altman announced his company will not go public this year, citing safety concerns.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/250c1f6a-b03d-11f1-a354-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/IA-Trump-thumbnail.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/250c1f6a-b03d-11f1-a354-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/IA-Trump-thumbnail.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a9e5ef7a-b03a-11f1-8323-ef2e14cb1ebe</guid><pubDate>Mon, 14 Sep 2026 12:49:02 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>US hosts G20 energy talks in Texas as Iran war disrupts global fuel markets</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260914-us-g20-energy-talks-iran-war</link><description>
The United States begins G20 meetings in Houston on Monday promoting “energy abundance” as President Donald Trump’s war against Iran disrupts global fuel markets. Delegations from major economies, including China, India, Japan and Germany, will attend alongside oil producers Canada and Saudi Arabia. Russia is also expected to participate.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/481134d6-a5bc-11f1-b352-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/58a2a20e7d0248e924993791c7981e68d2924bcc.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/481134d6-a5bc-11f1-b352-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/58a2a20e7d0248e924993791c7981e68d2924bcc.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5f4b68e0-afd2-11f1-90c1-3126f5b87fe4</guid><pubDate>Mon, 14 Sep 2026 01:42:29 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/481134d6-a5bc-11f1-b352-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/58a2a20e7d0248e924993791c7981e68d2924bcc.jpg">© Allison Joyce, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>‘I gave up my life to care for my father’: How 9/11 shaped a son’s sense of duty and life trajectory</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/i-gave-up-my-life-to-care-for-my-father-how-9-11-shaped-a-son-s-sense-of-duty-and-life-trajectory</link><description>
Jean-Emile Jammine is pleased to welcome Alessandro Stravato, a witness to the attacks of September 11th. His testimony offers a deeply personal account. He witnessed firsthand the second plane strike the World Trade Center from Arthur Ashe Stadium. Stravato’s first instinct was not to interpret the historical significance, just find his father, who was working at City Hall.  He found him alive, covered in debris and soot, trekking dozens of blocks through Manhattan. And while his father did survive, his health seriously deteriorated over the years. By 2015, as Alessandro's dad was losing his battle with cancer, he told his son to "stay strong."
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c1750c66-af8b-11f1-a643-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260911-225957-230927-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c1750c66-af8b-11f1-a643-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260911-225957-230927-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c6b28db6-af8b-11f1-a769-238242ee63f1</guid><pubDate>Sun, 13 Sep 2026 17:10:59 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>‘We did what we had to do’: 25 years on, 9/11 first responder reflects on duty, survival and family</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/we-did-what-we-had-to-do-25-years-on-9-11-first-responder-reflects-on-duty-survival-and-family</link><description>
Jean-Emile Jammine is pleased to welcome LaZetta Duncan, Retired NYPD Detective, 9/11 First Responder. Duncan remembers Ground Zero not as a historical event frozen in time, but as living history whose consequences continue to unfold and evolve 25 years on. Her testimony traces a striking progression: from the confusion and urgency of the attacks, rescue and recovery, to the grim transformation of gathering human remains and evidence inside a burning toxic apocalyptic crime scene. And we now learn of the overwhelming health consequences borne by responders despite repeated assurances that the air quality posed no health threat.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/202b85fe-af88-11f1-acf1-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260911-212958-214148-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/202b85fe-af88-11f1-acf1-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260911-212958-214148-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2562fb24-af88-11f1-9a33-1d982ffe8823</guid><pubDate>Sun, 13 Sep 2026 16:18:01 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Brazil: Michelle Bolsonaro's key role in the presidential race</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/brazil-michelle-bolsonaro-s-key-role-in-the-presidential-race</link><description>
Brazil is heading to the polls on October 4, with President Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva seeking a fourth term as the Bolsonaro family mounts a political comeback through Flávio's presidential bid and Michelle's Senate campaign. With polls pointing to another tight race, Michelle's popularity among women could prove crucial as the family tries to return to power.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7ece2006-af62-11f1-9504-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260913-120821-121000-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7ece2006-af62-11f1-9504-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260913-120821-121000-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">83e41de8-af62-11f1-a945-0121a29fa1cc</guid><pubDate>Sun, 13 Sep 2026 11:08:22 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>The week in pictures: 9/11 anniversary, far-right win in Germany and Houthis' Yemen offensive</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260913-the-week-in-pictures-9-11-anniversary-far-right-win-germany-houthis-yemen-offensive</link><description>
A look back at some of the week's key news stories and the most striking images, from commemorations marking 25 years since the 9/11 attacks to the breakthrough win for Germany's far-right AfD party and the lightening offensive that has left Yemen's Iran-backed Houthi rebels in control of the country's Red Sea coast.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9ae8a078-adc2-11f1-b7b9-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C7YH9LY.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9ae8a078-adc2-11f1-b7b9-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C7YH9LY.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a126d980-adec-11f1-88fe-45e2e454489d</guid><pubDate>Sun, 13 Sep 2026 10:48:49 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9ae8a078-adc2-11f1-b7b9-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C7YH9LY.jpg">© Leonardo Munoz, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Macron, Carney to visit North Atlantic French islands after Trump's map post</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260913-macron-carney-to-visit-french-islands-after-trump-s-map-post</link><description>
French President Emmanuel Macron and Canadian Prime Minister Mark Carney will reaffirm the “sovereignty of nations” on a visit on September 20 to Saint-Pierre-et-Miquelon, a French territory in the North Atlantic, the Élysée Palace announced on Sunday. The symbolic trip comes after US President Donald Trump posted a map on social media showing the entire North American continent covered by the US flag.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/07123c12-af55-11f1-9ad5-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/df646ee48064e65458879e443f4be68f8b225f7d.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/07123c12-af55-11f1-9ad5-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/df646ee48064e65458879e443f4be68f8b225f7d.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">08b45cd0-af55-11f1-a91e-e5cb8c8e2679</guid><pubDate>Sun, 13 Sep 2026 09:25:16 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/07123c12-af55-11f1-9ad5-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/df646ee48064e65458879e443f4be68f8b225f7d.jpg">© Evelyn Hockstein, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Spotlight</category><title>On Sept 12th, 'everyone was compassionate': The world needs 'to be together again' - Richard Roeill</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260913-on-sept-12th-everyone-was-compassionate-the-world-needs-to-be-together-again-richard-roeill</link><description>
FRANCE 24’s François Picard talks to Richard Roeill, former New York Firefighter and 9/11 First Responder. Roeill’s testimony reframes the legacy of September 11th not as a historical event confined to a single day, but as living history. The former New York City firefighter describes an anniversary that reactivates trauma, while the illnesses suffered by first responders make the consequences of Ground Zero ever-present decades later. He says that responders were misled about the dangers they faced and demands accountability and long-term healthcare for those exposed to the toxic air.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b09ae3ac-af40-11f1-8f49-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-4831165916aa649db9d44f8-98355403.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b09ae3ac-af40-11f1-8f49-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-4831165916aa649db9d44f8-98355403.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4e37993c-af43-11f1-9f8f-4f396abe40f0</guid><pubDate>Sun, 13 Sep 2026 07:18:22 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>François PICARD</dc:creator></item><item><category>The World This Week</category><title>Can we slow down AI, and who has the right to remember 9/11?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-world-this-week/20260911-can-we-slowdown-ai-and-9-11-who-has-the-right-to-remember</link><description>
In a week that marks 25 years since 9/11, Americans paused to pay tribute. Six bells tolled to signify six fatal moments in New York, at the Pentagon and in Pennsylvania– with a seventh bell rung this year to commemorate those who later died from 9/11-related illnesses.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ebcc439a-ae0e-11f1-86c2-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/WhatsApp-Image-2026-09-11-at-20-12-19.jpeg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ebcc439a-ae0e-11f1-86c2-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/WhatsApp-Image-2026-09-11-at-20-12-19.jpeg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7f09f986-ae05-11f1-8831-3d527545dca5</guid><pubDate>Fri, 11 Sep 2026 18:43:53 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Gavin LEE</dc:creator></item><item><category>Spotlight</category><title>US government has decided on 'Guantanamo forever'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260911-spotlight</link><description>
In this edition, FRANCE 24’s Gavin Lee speaks to New York Times reporter Carol Rosenberg, widely regarded as one of the foremost American journalists covering the US detention camp at Guantanamo Bay in Cuba. Several alleged suspects in the 9/11 attacks are still being held there, including their so-called “architect”, Khalid Sheikh Mohammed. He is scheduled for trial in June 2028, 27 years after the tragedy. To mark the anniversary, Rosenberg has written a reflective piece titled A Place Where Memories Have Faded Away.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b7aa6a36-ae0b-11f1-af27-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C82H8H8.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b7aa6a36-ae0b-11f1-af27-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C82H8H8.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e77bcd60-ae04-11f1-9883-49544767a90a</guid><pubDate>Fri, 11 Sep 2026 18:42:54 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Gavin LEE</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Flavio Bolsonaro probed for corruption as Brazil election tightens</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260911-flavio-bolsonaro-probed-for-corruption-as-brazil-election-tightens</link><description>
Just weeks before the vote, Brazilian presidential hopeful Flavio Bolsonaro's campaign is being rocked by revelations he is under investigation for alleged corruption and money laundering. The probe centres on financing sought for a film about his father, former president Jair Bolsonaro, court documents unsealed on Friday showed.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/60346ac2-adf7-11f1-98bc-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-09T171741Z-1887204671-RC2RFNA2JH7L-RTRMADP-3-BRAZIL-ELECTION-BOLSONARO.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/60346ac2-adf7-11f1-98bc-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-09T171741Z-1887204671-RC2RFNA2JH7L-RTRMADP-3-BRAZIL-ELECTION-BOLSONARO.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b070e5a8-adfa-11f1-9d66-817a00b83769</guid><pubDate>Fri, 11 Sep 2026 16:21:38 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/60346ac2-adf7-11f1-98bc-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-09T171741Z-1887204671-RC2RFNA2JH7L-RTRMADP-3-BRAZIL-ELECTION-BOLSONARO.jpg">© Pilar Olivares, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Trump delivers remarks at Pentagon ceremony to mark 25th anniversary of 9/11</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260911-trump-delivers-remarks-at-pentagon-ceremony-to-mark-25th-anniversary-of-9-11</link><description>
US President Donald Trump observed Friday’s 25th anniversary by speaking about 9/11 at a ceremony at the Pentagon commemorating the lives lost when al-Qaeda militants hijacked planes and killed nearly 3,000 people in three locations, upending American foreign policy and national security.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3239c8d6-adf4-11f1-b7bf-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/trumpmini.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3239c8d6-adf4-11f1-b7bf-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/trumpmini.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4cc3104a-adf4-11f1-b948-8b0afeaba68e</guid><pubDate>Fri, 11 Sep 2026 15:29:15 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>25 years after 9/11, al Qaeda remains a threat – even as Washington looks away</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260911-25-years-after-9-11-al-qaeda-remains-threat-washington-looks-away-counter-terrorism</link><description>
A quarter of a century after the deadliest terrorist attacks in US history, al Qaeda’s various branches have moved away from the global jihad advocated by Osama bin Laden, focusing instead on regional insurgencies. Their actions continue to destabilise swathes of the world, from the Sahel to Afghanistan, neglected by a US administration that critics say has unlearned the lessons of 9/11.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fcc9c0b8-ad29-11f1-9521-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP18340343104699.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fcc9c0b8-ad29-11f1-9521-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP18340343104699.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">99e5bb08-ade4-11f1-a201-abb2482cd37a</guid><pubDate>Fri, 11 Sep 2026 14:24:25 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fcc9c0b8-ad29-11f1-9521-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP18340343104699.jpg">© Farah Abdi Warsameh, AP file photo</source><dc:creator>Antoine FLANDRIN</dc:creator></item><item><category>Scoop</category><title>How the media has changed since 9/11</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/scoop/20260911-how-the-media-has-changed-since-9-11</link><description>
It has been 25 years since terrorists hijacked planes and flew them into the Twin Towers, the Pentagon, and a fourth crashed in a field in Pennsylvania. Nearly 3,000 people were killed in the attacks that changed the course of US and world history. This week FRANCE 24's media show Scoop looks at how journalists covered 9/11 and how the attacks changed the news industry.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/61d790fa-ade5-11f1-b615-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-5942620636aa4032c26b368-44973480.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/61d790fa-ade5-11f1-b615-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-5942620636aa4032c26b368-44973480.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b93df6b4-ade4-11f1-929d-abb2482cd37a</guid><pubDate>Fri, 11 Sep 2026 13:37:44 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>William HILDERBRANDT</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Vance calls Democrats 'party of hatred' as he seizes MAGA spotlight</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260911-vance-tries-label-democrats-as-party-of-hatred-seizes-maga-spotlight</link><description>
US Vice President JD Vance launched a virulent attack on the Democratic Party Thursday, accusing them of being the "party of hatred" at day two of the Republican convention ahead of the November midterm elections. With public support for President Donald Trump at record lows, Republican figures are increasingly trying to frame their opponents as dangerous political extremists.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4b830b4a-ada4-11f1-ad78-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26254075475865.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4b830b4a-ada4-11f1-ad78-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26254075475865.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">01f37ddc-ada6-11f1-a8c9-0d85900713cb</guid><pubDate>Fri, 11 Sep 2026 06:45:36 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4b830b4a-ada4-11f1-ad78-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26254075475865.jpg">© Julia Demaree Nikhinson, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>'That's why we fight': The US marks 25 years since 9/11 attacks</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260911-trump-new-york-25-years-9-11-muslim-mayor</link><description>
New York on Friday marked the 25th anniversary of the September 11, 2001 attacks, with US President Donald Trump attending a ceremony at the Pentagon while Vice President JD Vance and four former presidents joined commemorations at Ground Zero, where victims’ relatives will read the names of those killed.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6b04ed90-ade4-11f1-971b-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26254445189867.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6b04ed90-ade4-11f1-971b-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26254445189867.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f612de0c-ad7f-11f1-a9cf-5ddc1bb97edb</guid><pubDate>Fri, 11 Sep 2026 01:47:42 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6b04ed90-ade4-11f1-971b-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26254445189867.jpg">© Dave Sanders, The New York Times via AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Truth or Fake</category><title>Meta tests out putting fact-checking in users’ hands across Latin America</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/meta-tests-out-putting-fact-checking-in-users-hands-across-latin-america-1</link><description>
Meta is expanding its shift away from professional fact-checking. The tech giant announced it's trialling it's crowdsourced "Community Notes" system across 16 countries in Latin America. Meta says the system will only fully roll out once it is confident it works, but critics warn that with misinformation, manipulated images and AI-generated content spreading rapidly, crowdsourced checks may come too late to prevent false claims from reaching millions. Vedika Bahl explains the risks.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bc86acb0-ad50-11f1-baa9-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-12835300406aa309c93f4154-74074622.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bc86acb0-ad50-11f1-baa9-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-12835300406aa309c93f4154-74074622.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1d5c19aa-ad4f-11f1-8947-39b0630bb3ec</guid><pubDate>Thu, 10 Sep 2026 20:11:31 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Vedika BAHL</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>As New York marks 25 years since 9/11, Muslims recall stigmatisation in aftermath of attacks</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/as-new-york-marks-25-years-since-9-11-muslims-recall-stigmatization-in-aftermath-of-attacks</link><description>
As New York marks 25 years since the terrorist attacks on September 11th, New York’s Muslim community has become increasingly part of the fabric of the city. One sign of that is the election of Zohran Mamdani as the city’s mayor last November. Another is the state's largest mosque, due to open its doors at the end of the year. But while things have improved, many Muslims still remember the difficult months that followed the attack. FRANCE 24's Monte Francis reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/05bcffd2-11c1-11ec-9063-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000_9MG36Z.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/05bcffd2-11c1-11ec-9063-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000_9MG36Z.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ace33aca-ad4c-11f1-9f80-39b0630bb3ec</guid><pubDate>Thu, 10 Sep 2026 19:32:33 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>The Debate</category><title>9/11 then and now: Do September 2001 attacks still shape our world?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260910-9-11-then-and-now-do-september-2001-attacks-still-shape-our-world</link><description>
Once in a generation – sometimes once in a lifetime – a singular event blindsides the entire planet. 25 years on, does the memory of the 9/11 attacks on New York's Twin Towers, the Pentagon and in Pennsylvania fade into history, or is it still as raw and vivid as on that sunny September morning? 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a2e30182-ad41-11f1-8a5c-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-10T000955Z-1465141223-RC2YFNAS0O3V-RTRMADP-3-USA-SEPT11-MEMORIAL.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a2e30182-ad41-11f1-8a5c-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-10T000955Z-1465141223-RC2YFNAS0O3V-RTRMADP-3-USA-SEPT11-MEMORIAL.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fd16ebdc-ad41-11f1-9846-39e6bfb413de</guid><pubDate>Thu, 10 Sep 2026 18:17:34 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>François PICARD</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>What to know about Trump's pledge of $5,000 to 'every American' if GOP wins midterms</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260910-what-to-know-about-trump-s-5-000-dividend-pledge</link><description>
President Donald Trump ⁠promised a $5,000 "Trump dividend" ​payment to every US adult on Wednesday if his Republicans retain control of the House of Representatives and the Senate in the November 3 midterm elections. The pledge has raised numerous questions. Here's what we know so far. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/88cf8642-ad3e-11f1-a644-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/b62211bb909886fc2d314fba0eb844aa0f37ca66.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/88cf8642-ad3e-11f1-a644-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/b62211bb909886fc2d314fba0eb844aa0f37ca66.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8aa4d2e2-ad3e-11f1-a538-8fbd31854a2a</guid><pubDate>Thu, 10 Sep 2026 17:39:13 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/88cf8642-ad3e-11f1-a644-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/b62211bb909886fc2d314fba0eb844aa0f37ca66.jpg">© Ronaldo Schemidt, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Focus</category><title>Montserrat: The 'Pompeii' of the Caribbean</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20260910-montserrat-the-pompeii-of-the-caribbean</link><description>
Part of the island of Montserrat, a UK Overseas Territory, was buried by a volcanic eruption in 1995. Today, caution is essential for those venturing on the mysterious island that is full of spectacular Caribbean landscapes. Our colleagues at France Télévisions and FRANCE 24's Florent Marchais report.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d114d97c-ac4c-11f1-a0d7-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/montserrat-volcano-frz-focus.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d114d97c-ac4c-11f1-a0d7-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/montserrat-volcano-frz-focus.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">55320db0-ac52-11f1-99f2-515e3382455e</guid><pubDate>Thu, 10 Sep 2026 13:58:36 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE 2</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Colombia court orders President de la Espriella to hide social media videos of him with dead bodies</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260910-colombia-court-orders-president-de-la-espriella-to-hide-social-media-videos-of-him-with-dead-bodies</link><description>
Colombia's right-wing President Abelardo de la Espriella has been ordered to hide social media videos showing him walking past rows of the dead bodies of alleged guerrillas killed by the country's armed forces, according to a court document seen Wednesday. The newly sworn-in president has launched a fresh offensive at armed groups involved in the country's lucrative cocaine trade. 
